# Cloned upstream sources — read-only study copies, never committed.
# They belong to their own projects and would bloat this repo's history.
upstream/*
!upstream/README.md
!upstream/repos.txt

# GSD planning workspace — session-local codebase maps and planning state,
# regenerable via /gsd-map-codebase; not part of the repo's public record.
.planning/

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
# Downloaded papers — read-only study copies, never committed.
# Copyright belongs to the publishers; refetchable from each note's arxiv/doi frontmatter.
references/papers/pdf/*
!references/papers/pdf/.gitkeep

# Cached vendor model cards. NOT refetchable the way a paper is — a card is rewritten in
# place at one URL — which is why every card note carries a REQUIRED snapshot: (Wayback)
# URL. The note plus its snapshot is the record; this copy is a convenience.
references/cards/pdf/*
!references/cards/pdf/.gitkeep
# Generated SQLite export of the corpus — a VIEW over frontmatter, never authoritative
# (ADR-0035). Rebuilt from scratch in under a second by scripts/build-db.py, so it is
# never worth committing and never worth repairing: delete and rebuild.
comparisons/repo.db

# Probe wire evidence (Phase 9, D-09 one-way-door checkpoint). RESEARCH/ARCHITECTURE's
# default was "committed, not gitignored" (dated primary evidence, like experiments/
# logs); on 2026-09-01 the owner declined that default provisionally, revisit gate
# named as Phase 11. That revisit happened 2026-09-02 (Phase 11 plan 11-06, D-04's
# revisit gate): the owner decided to commit, verbatim "I think i am ok with these
# informations being public" — given after (a) confirming via `gh repo view` that
# this repo is currently PUBLIC, so committing publishes the evidence immediately,
# not provisionally, and (b) reviewing one full raw record per vendor (all 8) in
# session, with the two things a public reader would learn flagged explicitly:
# API-account rate-limit tiers (`x-ratelimit-limit-tokens` etc.) and the probing
# server's rough region via CDN routing headers (CF-RAY PRG / X-Amz-Cf-Pop FRA56).
# `probes/audit-evidence.py --check` is the fail-closed gate every future evidence
# commit passes (D-05; wired into CLAUDE.md's pre-commit lint battery below) — a
# finding blocks the commit until the evidence itself is fixed, never by narrowing
# the scanner. Full context: probes/PREREGISTRATION.md's Run log, 2026-09-02 entry.
# probes/harness/ (code) and probes/sets/ (declarations) were never covered by this
# rule and always committed normally.

__pycache__/
